{"title":"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/c/cfc90becf098dcd7b505c70b0717df2a28e5ccdd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(z) = z^8 + \\left(4\\sqrt{3} + 6\\right)z^4 - \\left(4\\sqrt{3} + 7\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"311\" height=\"32\" />. What is the minimum perimeter among all the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-sided polygons in the complex plane whose vertices are precisely the zeros of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/0/9e048a9db04ffc89eec3e0d78777919f12df3aeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/4/b84f4e7b3791d1b75100b2eb550a8bb7305713d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 4\\sqrt{3} + 4 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 8\\sqrt{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\  3\\sqrt{2} + 3\\sqrt{6} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\  4\\sqrt{2} + 4\\sqrt{3} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\  4\\sqrt{3} + 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"643\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Answer: (B)\n</p><p>First of all, we need to find all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />  such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/d/71dcb6eb815a761a204742591ffe23f28edf4877.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(z) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/8/8781ed134ad638ea69e4c5e14f11d4c322a871f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(z) = \\left(z^4 - 1\\right)\\left(z^4 + \\left(4\\sqrt{3} + 7\\right)\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"272\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/4/844533a1f0c664955217520b1f02c0e9d1b7803b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^4 = 1 \\implies z =  e^{i\\frac{n\\pi}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"167\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/2/2d20e8f09874786c2d9b4909a698ce6a447f7275.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^4 = - \\left(4\\sqrt{3} + 7\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"141\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/7/29758780c55b6e9161bd614a00882257a50805f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^2 = \\pm i \\sqrt{4\\sqrt{3} + 7} = e^{i\\frac{(2n+1)\\pi}{2}} \\left(\\sqrt{3} + 2\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"311\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/7/f877bb702c60d75538232145751bc3b20cd422ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = e^{i\\frac{(2n+1)\\pi}{4}} \\sqrt{\\sqrt{3} + 2} = e^{i\\frac{(2n+1)\\pi}{4}} \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{2}} + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"359\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>Now we have a solution at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/8/058e4191a627fa4f4397c9aa94dccad0c76dca84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n\\pi}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"33\" /> if we look at them in polar coordinate, further more, the 8-gon is symmetric (it is an equilateral octagon) . So we only need to find the side length of one and multiply by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>So answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/8/cb8a2403c2901926422c536ac1fc058de52c5cd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 8 \\times$\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" /> distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/0/a709ea71c76fba586043f06e06c8b1aec0448088.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} + \\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\left(1 + i\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"148\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p>Side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/c/89cb171a4d859bee111845bfc58e07fee34112af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} - \\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} + \\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2} = \\sqrt{2\\left(\\frac{3}{4} + \\frac{1}{4}\\right)} = \\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -24px\" width=\"436\" height=\"64\" />\n</p><p>Hence, answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ada42b1f945fea827946e80d64ab5f27e7ba8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Use the law of cosines.\nWe make <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> the distance.\nNow, since the angle does not change the distance from the origin, we can just use the distance. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/4/e54643af2eea01a7ec6c7cc2d3e70bd135a3f2ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 = (\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{2}} + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}})^2 + 1^2 -2 \\times \\Big( \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{2}} + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\Big)\\times 1 \\times \\cos \\frac{\\pi}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"428\" height=\"45\" />, which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/9/ef97fb70f4484d4df9e03ede91c26ae4f6100d0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2= 2 + \\sqrt3 +1 - 1 - \\sqrt3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"206\" height=\"18\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/b/35bea2ea08cd6bb94fcc17281ccd11aa5969282f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2=2$\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/e/2be98244455ccefb960e5c13f409cca2cd5ecb64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\sqrt2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" />.\nMultiply the answer by 8 to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/1/f8160ee7ec6931a8af19e10d73ec41fc008ac64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{ (B) 8\\sqrt2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"74\" height=\"33\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B\">2011 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">Problem 25</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"tex